<title>Pocket AI Sphere</title>
<meta name="claude:viewport-fit-sides" content="cover">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wght@500;700;900&family=Public+Sans:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;0,700;1,400&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;700&display=swap">
<style>:root{
  --bg:#EDEBE7; --paper:#FFFFFF; --ink:#16181C; --ink-2:#5A6068; --line:#CFCBC4;
  --brass:#8F6114; --brass-soft:#F2E6D2; --signal:#0E5F7A; --signal-soft:#D9EAF1;
  --ok:#2A6340; --ok-soft:#D9EADF; --warn:#98351E; --warn-soft:#F7E1D9;
  --mono:"JetBrains Mono",ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;
  --display:"Archivo","Helvetica Neue",Arial,sans-serif;
  --body:"Public Sans","Segoe UI",system-ui,sans-serif;
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){
  :root:not([data-theme="light"]){
    --bg:#14161A; --paper:#1D2026; --ink:#E8E6E2; --ink-2:#9BA3AC; --line:#333841;
    --brass:#D69A4E; --brass-soft:#3A2C18; --signal:#5BB8D4; --signal-soft:#15323D;
    --ok:#6FBF8E; --ok-soft:#1A3325; --warn:#EE8666; --warn-soft:#3B1D14; color-scheme:dark;
  }
}
:root[data-theme="dark"]{
  --bg:#14161A; --paper:#1D2026; --ink:#E8E6E2; --ink-2:#9BA3AC; --line:#333841;
  --brass:#D69A4E; --brass-soft:#3A2C18; --signal:#5BB8D4; --signal-soft:#15323D;
  --ok:#6FBF8E; --ok-soft:#1A3325; --warn:#EE8666; --warn-soft:#3B1D14; color-scheme:dark;
}
*{box-sizing:border-box}
body{background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font-family:var(--body);font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;margin:0}
.wrap{max-width:920px;margin:0 auto;padding-left:max(16px,env(safe-area-inset-left,0px));padding-right:max(16px,env(safe-area-inset-right,0px));padding-block:28px 72px}
h1,h2,h3{font-family:var(--display);text-wrap:balance;line-height:1.1;margin:0}
h1{font-size:clamp(30px,6vw,46px);font-weight:900;letter-spacing:-0.015em}
h2{font-size:clamp(20px,3vw,26px);font-weight:700;margin:34px 0 8px}
p{margin:10px 0;max-width:72ch}
ul,ol{max-width:72ch;padding-left:22px;margin:10px 0}
li{margin:7px 0}
a{color:var(--signal)}
code{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.88em;background:var(--signal-soft);padding:1.5px 5px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap}
strong{font-weight:700}
.masthead{border-bottom:4px solid var(--ink);padding-bottom:18px;margin-bottom:8px}
.eyebrow{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);font-weight:700}
.sub{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);margin-top:10px;line-height:1.5}
figure{margin:22px 0;background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;padding:12px;overflow-x:auto}
figure svg{max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;font-family:var(--body)}
figcaption{font-size:14px;color:var(--ink-2);margin-top:10px;max-width:72ch;line-height:1.5}
.grid3{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px}
.grid3 figure{margin:0;min-width:0}
@media (max-width:700px){.grid3{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
.kpis{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:10px;margin:22px 0}
.kpis div{background:var(--brass-soft);border:1px solid var(--brass);border-radius:6px;padding:12px 14px;min-width:0}
.kpis b{display:block;font-family:var(--display);font-size:24px;font-weight:900;color:var(--brass)}
.kpis span{font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2)}
@media (max-width:600px){.kpis{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}
.tw{overflow-x:auto;margin:12px 0}
table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14.5px}
th,td{text-align:left;padding:8px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);vertical-align:top}
th{font-family:var(--display);font-size:12.5px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--ink-2)}
td:first-child{white-space:nowrap}
.badge{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;padding:2px 7px;border-radius:999px;white-space:nowrap}
.badge.own{background:var(--ok-soft);color:var(--ok)}
.badge.buy{background:var(--warn-soft);color:var(--warn)}
.badge.opt{background:var(--signal-soft);color:var(--signal)}
.note{padding:13px 17px;margin:18px 0;border-radius:5px}
.note p,.note ul{max-width:none;margin:5px 0}
.note .lbl{display:block;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:5px;font-weight:700}
.warn{background:var(--warn-soft);border:1px solid var(--warn)}
.warn .lbl{color:var(--warn)}
.tip{background:var(--signal-soft);border:1px solid var(--signal)}
.tip .lbl{color:var(--signal)}
hr{border:0;border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:44px 0 0}
/* Rev B: the parts' own colours (no paint, no skins) */
:root{--blk:#1E2024;--blk-lo:#0B0C0E;--blue:#2B5BA8;--chrome:#C9CDD3;--px:#F4F4F0;--wrap:#161718;--yellow:#D9A400;--white:#F6F5F1;--glass:#0B0C0E}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){:root:not([data-theme="light"]){--blk:#2A2D33;--blk-lo:#15171A;--blue:#3F74C9;--chrome:#B8BDC4;--white:#ECEAE4;--glass:#060708}}
:root[data-theme="dark"]{--blk:#2A2D33;--blk-lo:#15171A;--blue:#3F74C9;--chrome:#B8BDC4;--white:#ECEAE4;--glass:#060708}
.grid2{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px}
.grid2 figure{margin:0;min-width:0}
@media (max-width:700px){.grid2{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
.changes li{margin:9px 0}
figure.sheet{padding:6px}
</style>
<div class="wrap">
<div class="masthead">
  <div class="eyebrow">Pocket AI &middot; third build &middot; Rev B, approved as drawn 2026-11-10</div>
  <h1>A Pocket AI in a brass sphere</h1>
  <div class="sub">Same assistant as the first Pocket AI, plus a camera and a weather sensor, in three brass rings. Step one of the build rule, approved as drawn on 2026-11-10; step two, the physics, is the companion page. Nothing bent, soldered or flashed; one board in the mail. Source: <code>pocket_ai_sphere/docs/DESIGN.md</code>, drawn by <code>docs/pages/gen/sphere.py</code>.</div>
</div>

<p>Three rings and two posts. An equator and a side ring of 1.5&nbsp;mm brass rod cross at left and right, so the front and back are open; a 44 mm base ring under them is what it stands on and what the cell tray rests on. Two thin posts rise from the base ring through the screen's mounting holes and carry the XIAO above it. That is the whole frame: five joints, two ties, two hooks. The screen sits below the equator and the camera above it, so the equator reads as a brow. The heavy cell lies on the floor as ballast with the speaker lying on it, firing up; the sensor hangs from the top in moving air. The two blue parts, the amplifier and the toggle's body, stand in the gap behind the screen where nothing sees them; the chrome lever, a white button cap and one white wire bundle are the only things that are not brass or black.</p>

<figure><svg viewBox="0 0 960 640" role="img" aria-label="Three-quarter view of the three-ring brass sphere with the OLED face below the equator, the camera above it, the cell low with the speaker on it, the sensor at the top">
<text x="18" y="24" font-size="13.5" font-weight="700" fill="var(--ink)">The sphere from the front right. 70 mm across; 5.2 px per mm. Rev B, 2026-11-10.</text>
