<div class="kpis">
<div><b>70 mm</b><span>diameter; a tennis ball is 67</span></div>
<div><b>58 g</b><span>estimated, cell in</span></div>
<div><b>3.4 h</b><span>streaming and talking; 7.8 h idle</span></div>
<div><b>10 h</b><span>to charge through the XIAO's USB-C, asleep</span></div>
</div>

<h2>What changed from Rev A</h2>
<ul class="changes"><li><strong>The screen moved below the equator and the camera above it.</strong> In Rev A the equator ran across the eyes 17 mm in front of the glass. Now the OLED sits at y −24.5 to 2.5 with the equator crossing only its pin strip, and the XIAO sits at y 5 to 23 with the lens on the eye line: the equator reads as a brow between them.</li><li><strong>The speaker stood below the floor.</strong> Rev A taped it under the tray at y −32, 5 mm below the base ring the sphere stands on. It now lies across the cell on the tray's walls, firing up through the open top, and from behind it hides the amplifier's top edge.</li><li><strong>The posts no longer touch any pin.</strong> Rev A soldered the boards' header pins to the posts, which would have tied the OLED's four pins together. The posts now pass through the OLED's four mounting holes (23 mm pitch) and the XIAO's short edges are glued to them. The frame stays floating, as on the first Pocket AI.</li><li><strong>The AHT20 hangs on hooks, not pads.</strong> Rev A soldered its two outer pads (VIN and SDA) to the ring. Two 1.0 mm J-hooks through its front mounting holes do it now.</li><li><strong>Colour audit under the no-paint, no-cover rule.</strong> The blue amplifier and the blue toggle body stand in the gap behind the screen, out of sight; the chrome lever, the white button cap and one white wire bundle are what shows. No fish paper, no heat-shrink sleeves, no skins.</li><li><strong>The wiring sheet is new</strong>, with every pin, the nets, the power chain, run time and charge time.</li><li><strong>USB-C to the left.</strong> Rotated that way, the XIAO's bottom row carries the I2S and I2C pins next to the screen and the amp, and its top row the 3V3 and GND for the sensor above.</li><li><strong>The XIAO count corrected.</strong> Rev A said three were owned; the sphere's board is in the pair expected by 11-15.</li></ul>

<h2>Colour, part by part</h2>
<p>The rule of 2026-11-09: no paint and no covers; parts in brass, ivory, white or black, and anything sold only in another colour placed out of sight. Nothing here is skinned, sleeved or sprayed.</p>
<div class="tw"><table class=""><tr><th>Part</th><th>Colour as sold</th><th>Where it sits</th><th>What shows</th></tr><tr><td>Brass rings, posts, ties, hooks</td><td>brass</td><td>the whole outline</td><td>brass, its own colour</td></tr><tr><td>OLED</td><td>black glass, white pixels; board colour to check in the drawer</td><td>the face, below the equator, on the posts</td><td>glass and pixels; the pin strip behind the equator line</td></tr><tr><td>XIAO ESP32-S3 Sense</td><td>black boards, silver shield, black camera</td><td>above the equator, the lens at eye line</td><td>black</td></tr><tr><td>AHT20</td><td>black</td><td>flat under the top of the side ring</td><td>black, edge-on from the front</td></tr><tr><td>Amplifier (HiLetgo)</td><td>blue; Adafruit's is blue too</td><td>against the back of the screen, in the 11 mm gap</td><td>nothing from the front or the back; a 3 mm edge from the sides</td></tr><tr><td>Toggle (MTS-102)</td><td>blue body, chrome bushing and lever</td><td>against the tray wall in the gap, lever out to the right</td><td>the chrome lever; its 13 x 10 mm end face from the right side only</td></tr><tr><td>Speaker</td><td>black</td><td>lying across the cell, firing up</td><td>black</td></tr><tr><td>Cell (NL169)</td><td>black and yellow wrap</td><td>in the tray on the floor</td><td>yellow lettering from the sides; the one off-palette thing in view</td></tr><tr><td>Cell tray</td><td>black plastic</td><td>across the base ring</td><td>black</td></tr><tr><td>Button</td><td>black body, white cap</td><td>inside the right joint</td><td>the white cap</td></tr><tr><td>220 µF</td><td>black can</td><td>behind the tray</td><td>black</td></tr><tr><td>Wires</td><td>white 26 and 30 AWG</td><td>one bundle down behind the boards</td><td>a white line</td></tr></table></div>

<h2>Why these numbers</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>70 mm</strong> is the smallest sphere that takes a 27 mm screen below the equator and the 21 mm XIAO above it, 19 mm forward of the centre, with the 43 mm tray across the floor. The screen's lower corners sit on the surface at y = −24.5, 2.7 mm above the base ring.</li>
<li><strong>Screen under the brow, camera over it.</strong> The equator is a rod at y = 0, 14 mm in front of the boards. Put the glass below it and the lens above it and the rod divides the face instead of crossing it. The equator passes only the screen's pin strip.</li>
<li><strong>One 300 mm rod per ring.</strong> A 70 mm circle is 220 mm around, so each big ring is one rod with an 80 mm offcut and no splice in view; the base ring is a third rod.</li>
<li><strong>The posts are the screen's own mounting holes.</strong> Four 2 mm holes on about a 23 mm pitch: two straight rods pass through them and the module cannot twist. The XIAO has no holes, so its short edges are glued to the same two rods, 0.5 mm away. No pin touches brass and the frame stays floating.</li>
<li><strong>An 11 mm gap behind the screen</strong> is what hides the two blue parts: the screen's board is 18 mm forward of the centre and the tray's front wall 6.5 mm, so the 8 mm toggle body stands against the wall and the 3 mm amplifier against the screen. Both sit above the screen's bottom edge and below the speaker's top, so neither the front nor the back sees them.</li>
<li><strong>Cell at y = −19</strong> puts 20 g of the 58 on the floor; that is what brings it back upright when you press the button.</li>
<li><strong>Sensor at the top, heat at the front.</strong> The AHT20 reads air, not the XIAO, because it sits 20 mm behind and 8 mm above the stack with open rods around it. Expect 1–2 °C of self-heating after an hour of streaming; the firmware subtracts a measured offset.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Parts</h2>
<p>Everything but the controller is in the drawers. The controller is in the pair Amazon expects by 11-15. Nothing to buy.</p>
<div class="tw"><table class="parts"><tr><th>Qty</th><th>Part</th><th>Where</th><th>Colour</th><th>Why, and what to check</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Seeed XIAO ESP32-S3 Sense<br><span class="badge opt">in the mail</span></td><td><a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0C69FFVHH">the pair ordered 2026-10-27, expected by 11-15</a></td><td>black boards, silver shield</td><td>The brain, the camera and the microphone. The family owns four: Crumb&#x27;s and the drone&#x27;s are due by 11-11, the pair for the camera Pocket AI and this sphere by 11-15 (Amazon Orders page, read 11-03; no shipping mail by 11-10). The one part not in a drawer.</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Hosyond SSD1306 0.96&quot; OLED, white pixels<br><span class="badge own">owned</span></td><td><a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B09T6SJBV5">owned x10</a></td><td>black glass; board colour to check</td><td>The face. I2C 0x3C on D4/D5. Read the silkscreen for the pin order before wiring. Its four 2 mm mounting holes are what the posts pass through: measure their pitch (about 23 mm) and set the posts to it. Open the drawer and check the board&#x27;s colour: the listing says only &#x27;white&#x27; for the pixels. If it is blue, the glass covers most of it and the pin strip sits behind the equator; a black-board 0.96&quot; module is the matching-colour buy if that is not enough.</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Adafruit AHT20 temperature + humidity, STEMMA QT<br><span class="badge own">owned</span></td><td><a href="https://www.adafruit.com/product/4566">owned x5, three spare</a></td><td>black</td><td>The weather sensor. I2C 0x38 on the same bus as the OLED; the address cannot change, so one per bus. 25.4 x 17.8 mm with four 2.5 mm holes on a 20.3 x 12.7 mm pattern (Adafruit&#x27;s fab print); it hangs from the side ring on two hooks through the two front holes. Header VIN, GND, SCL, SDA; the QT sockets stay empty.</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>HiLetgo MAX98357A amplifier<br><span class="badge own">owned</span></td><td><a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0CDWXZZCH">owned x12</a></td><td>blue, so out of sight</td><td>Runs from the cell (2.5-5.5 V in). SD held low by R1 until firmware raises it; GAIN open (9 dB); volume cap 65. Adafruit&#x27;s own board is blue too and out of stock, so no black one exists: this one stands against the back of the screen, above its bottom edge, where the screen hides it from the front and the tray, the cell and the speaker hide it from behind.</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Same Sky CES-20134-088PM speaker<br><span class="badge own">owned</span></td><td><a href="https://www.digikey.com/en/products/detail/same-sky-formerly-cui-devices/CES-20134-088PM/10821309">owned x6</a></td><td>black</td><td>Sealed 20 x 13 x 4.9 mm, 8 ohm, 0.8 W. Lies across the cell on the tray&#x27;s walls, taped to them, firing up through the open top; a 20 mm cone is all but omnidirectional at speech frequencies in an open frame, and from behind it is what hides the amplifier&#x27;s top edge. Neither lead to ground.</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Nitecore NL169 16340, protected<br><span class="badge own">owned</span></td><td><a href="https://imrbatteries.com/products/nitecore-nl169-16340-950mah-battery">owned x13</a></td><td>black and yellow wrap</td><td>The cell and the ballast: 950 mAh, 2 A protection, button top, 20 g lying across the floor. The one off-palette thing left in view: its yellow lettering shows from the sides between the rings. Hidden from the front by the screen and from behind by the speaker. Never solder to it.</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>ACEIRMC 16340 / CR123A holder with leads<br><span class="badge own">owned</span></td><td><a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0CRGK889F">owned x10</a></td><td>black</td><td>43 x 18 x 14 mm tray; the cell stands 2.6 mm proud of its walls. It lies across the 44 mm base ring, resting on it at both ends, tied down with two short white wire ties through the ring. Meter that red is the + contact.</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Ferwooh MTS-102 toggle switch<br><span class="badge own">owned</span></td><td><a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0CZ6XZ2P9">owned x20</a></td><td>blue body, chrome bushing and lever</td><td>Power switch in the cell&#x27;s + lead: the middle lug and one outer lug; the third stays empty. The rover found no black one, so here the body stands against the tray&#x27;s front wall behind the screen&#x27;s right half, below the cell&#x27;s top, and only the chrome bushing and lever show, poking out to the right of the screen&#x27;s lower edge. Lever forward is on.</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>QTEATAK tactile button, white cap<br><span class="badge own">owned</span></td><td><a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FHW6HMG4">owned x420</a></td><td>black body, white cap</td><td>The action button, glued to the inside of the right joint where the equator and the side ring cross, its white cap pointing out: press the sphere&#x27;s right pole.</td></tr><tr><td>1 + 1 + 2</td><td>R1 4.7 kΩ; 220 µF; 10 µF + 100 nF<br><span class="badge own">owned</span></td><td><a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0F4P352BB">LuminologyPro, ALLECIN, BOJACK kits</a></td><td>black can, tan ceramics</td><td>R1 amp SD pull-down; 220 µF across BAT+ and GND, standing behind the tray; 10 µF + 100 nF at the OLED&#x27;s VCC pin, behind the module.</td></tr><tr><td>3 rods</td><td>K&amp;S 1.5 mm brass rod, 300 mm<br><span class="badge own">owned</span></td><td><a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B005WPAW9M">owned (K&amp;S #9862 5-packs)</a></td><td>brass</td><td>One rod per ring: equator (220 mm), side ring (220 mm), base ring (138 mm). Solid rod bends to these radii without kinking; the 1.5 mm tube would.</td></tr><tr><td>1 rod</td><td>K&amp;S 1.0 mm brass rod, 300 mm<br><span class="badge own">owned</span></td><td><a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B005WPB7YG">owned (K&amp;S #9861 5-packs)</a></td><td>brass</td><td>Two posts (50 mm each), two ties to the equator (15 mm), two J-hooks for the AHT20 (12 mm): 154 mm of the rod.</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>26 AWG and 30 AWG silicone wire, white; Kapton<br><span class="badge own">owned</span></td><td><a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B073RDGTPB">owned (TUOFENG, CBAZY kits)</a></td><td>white</td><td>Every wire is white: 26 AWG for BAT+ and GND, 30 AWG for the eight signal wires, in one bundle down behind the boards. Kapton only on the XIAO&#x27;s back under its antenna. No fish paper and no heat-shrink sleeves: the tray is plastic and nothing is covered.</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>B-7000 glue<br><span class="badge own">owned</span></td><td><a href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=b-7000+glue">owned</a></td><td>clear</td><td>Eight dabs: the OLED&#x27;s four holes to the posts, the XIAO&#x27;s two short edges to the posts (two dabs each). Hot glue lets go of cold brass; B-7000 does not.</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>External 16340 charger (Nitecore UI1 or XTAR VC2)<br><span class="badge opt">optional</span></td><td><a href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=nitecore+ui1">optional, about $10-15</a></td><td></td><td>Two hours per cell instead of the XIAO&#x27;s ten. Not needed to build or run.</td></tr></table></div>

<h2>The wiring sheet</h2>
<figure class="sheet"><svg viewBox="0 0 1360 940" role="img" aria-label="Pocket AI Sphere wiring sheet"><style>.part{fill:var(--paper);stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1.6}.usb{fill:var(--line);stroke:var(--ink-2);stroke-width:1.2}.title{font:700 17px 'Archivo','Helvetica Neue',Arial,sans-serif;fill:var(--ink)}.sub{font:400 12px 'Public Sans',system-ui,sans-serif;fill:var(--ink-2)}.h1{font:900 24px 'Archivo','Helvetica Neue',Arial,sans-serif;fill:var(--ink)}.h2{font:700 15px 'Archivo','Helvetica Neue',Arial,sans-serif;fill:var(--ink)}.pin{font:700 13px 'JetBrains Mono',monospace;fill:var(--ink)}.fn{font:400 11.5px 'Public Sans',system-ui,sans-serif;fill:var(--ink-2)}.lab{font:700 12.5px 'Public Sans',system-ui,sans-serif;fill:var(--ink)}.mono{font:400 11.5px 'JetBrains Mono',monospace;fill:var(--ink)}.brass{font:700 12px 'JetBrains Mono',monospace;fill:var(--brass);letter-spacing:.08em}.rod{fill:none;stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:3.2;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round}.bus{fill:none;stroke:var(--brass);stroke-width:5;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round}.thin{fill:none;stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1.8;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round}.joint{fill:var(--ink)}.pinend{fill:var(--paper);stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1.8}</style><text x="20.0" y="30.0" class="h1" text-anchor="start" >Pocket AI Sphere: every connection on one sheet</text><text x="20.0" y="48.0" class="sub" text-anchor="start" >A dot is a joint. A line that hops over another does not touch it. Thick = wire you solder (26 AWG for BAT+ and GND, 30 AWG for the rest, all white).</text><text x="20.0" y="64.0" class="sub" text-anchor="start" >Thin = a resistor or capacitor leg, or a lead that comes with the part. Ground symbols are one net: the holder's − lead is the star. Nothing is soldered to brass.</text><rect x="560" y="140" width="300" height="500" rx="9" class="part"/><text x="710.0" y="430.0" class="title" text-anchor="middle" >XIAO ESP32-S3 Sense</text><text x="710.0" y="448.0" class="sub" text-anchor="middle" >black · camera GPIO10-18, 38-40, 47, 48 · PDM mic GPIO41/42</text><text x="710.0" y="464.0" class="sub" text-anchor="middle" >all inside the Sense board · SD slot stays empty</text><circle cx="560" cy="190" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="570.0" y="195.0" class="pin" text-anchor="start" >3V3</text><text x="610.0" y="195.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >3.3 V out, 700 mA</text><circle cx="560" cy="220" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="570.0" y="225.0" class="pin" text-anchor="start" >GND</text><text x="610.0" y="225.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >signal ground</text><circle cx="560" cy="250" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="570.0" y="255.0" class="pin" text-anchor="start" >D4</text><text x="610.0" y="255.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >GPIO5 · SDA</text><circle cx="560" cy="280" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="570.0" y="285.0" class="pin" text-anchor="start" >D5</text><text x="610.0" y="285.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >GPIO6 · SCL</text><circle cx="560" cy="540" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="570.0" y="545.0" class="pin" text-anchor="start" >D0</text><text x="610.0" y="545.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >GPIO1 · BCLK</text><circle cx="560" cy="570" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="570.0" y="575.0" class="pin" text-anchor="start" >D1</text><text x="610.0" y="575.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >GPIO2 · LRC</text><circle cx="560" cy="600" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="570.0" y="605.0" class="pin" text-anchor="start" >D2</text><text x="610.0" y="605.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >GPIO3 · DIN</text><circle cx="560" cy="630" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="570.0" y="635.0" class="pin" text-anchor="start" >D3</text><text x="610.0" y="635.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >GPIO4 · amp SD</text><circle cx="860" cy="190" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="850.0" y="195.0" class="pin" text-anchor="end" >D7</text><text x="810.0" y="195.0" class="fn" text-anchor="end" >GPIO44 · button</text><circle cx="860" cy="220" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="850.0" y="225.0" class="pin" text-anchor="end" >GND</text><text x="810.0" y="225.0" class="fn" text-anchor="end" >button return</text><text x="848.0" y="318.0" class="fn" text-anchor="end" >D6 = GPIO43: spare, leave free (UART TX)</text><text x="848.0" y="335.0" class="fn" text-anchor="end" >D8-D10 = GPIO7-9: spare, the SD slot's SPI</text><text x="848.0" y="352.0" class="fn" text-anchor="end" >5V pin: USB only · nothing connects here</text><text x="848.0" y="369.0" class="fn" text-anchor="end" >BAT pads: on the back, at the USB end</text><circle cx="760" cy="640" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="760.0" y="632.0" class="pin" text-anchor="start" transform="rotate(-90 760 632)">BAT+</text><circle cx="830" cy="640" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="830.0" y="632.0" class="pin" text-anchor="start" transform="rotate(-90 830 632)">BAT−</text><rect x="808" y="148" width="38" height="15" rx="3" class="usb"/><text x="827.0" y="159.0" class="fn" text-anchor="middle" >USB-C</text><text x="802.0" y="159.0" class="fn" text-anchor="end" >flash · console · charges the cell at 100 mA</text><rect x="1000" y="160" width="170" height="80" rx="9" class="part"/><text x="1085.0" y="192.0" class="title" text-anchor="middle" >Action button</text><text x="1085.0" y="210.0" class="sub" text-anchor="middle" >white cap · to GND</text><circle cx="1000" cy="190" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="1010.0" y="195.0" class="pin" text-anchor="start" ></text><circle cx="1000" cy="220" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="1010.0" y="225.0" class="pin" text-anchor="start" ></text><path d="M860.0,190.0 L1000.0,190.0" class="rod"/><path d="M860.0,220.0 L1000.0,220.0" class="rod"/><text x="930.0" y="182.0" class="lab" text-anchor="middle" >BTN</text><text x="930.0" y="212.0" class="lab" text-anchor="middle" >GND</text><path d="M560.0,190.0 L80.0,190.0" class="rod"/><path d="M560.0,220.0 L150.0,220.0" class="rod"/><path d="M560.0,250.0 L200.0,250.0" class="rod"/><path d="M560.0,280.0 L240.0,280.0" class="rod"/><text x="520.0" y="183.0" class="lab" text-anchor="middle" >3V3</text><text x="520.0" y="213.0" class="lab" text-anchor="middle" >GND</text><text x="520.0" y="243.0" class="lab" text-anchor="middle" >SDA</text><text x="520.0" y="273.0" class="lab" text-anchor="middle" >SCL</text><rect x="60" y="340" width="220" height="130" rx="9" class="part"/><text x="170.0" y="392.0" class="title" text-anchor="middle" >0.96" OLED</text><text x="170.0" y="410.0" class="sub" text-anchor="middle" >SSD1306 · I2C 0x3C · 3.3 V</text><text x="170.0" y="426.0" class="sub" text-anchor="middle" >read the silkscreen order first</text><circle cx="110" cy="340" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="110.0" y="348.0" class="pin" text-anchor="end" transform="rotate(-90 110 348)">VCC</text><path d="M110.0,340.0 L110.0,190.0" class="rod"/><circle cx="110.0" cy="190.0" r="6" class="joint"/><circle cx="150" cy="340" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="150.0" y="348.0" class="pin" text-anchor="end" transform="rotate(-90 150 348)">GND</text><path d="M150.0,340.0 L150.0,220.0" class="rod"/><circle cx="200" cy="340" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="200.0" y="348.0" class="pin" text-anchor="end" transform="rotate(-90 200 348)">SDA</text><path d="M200.0,340.0 L200.0,250.0" class="rod"/><circle cx="240" cy="340" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="240.0" y="348.0" class="pin" text-anchor="end" transform="rotate(-90 240 348)">SCL</text><path d="M240.0,340.0 L240.0,280.0" class="rod"/><path d="M80.0,190.0 L80.0,240.0" class="thin"/><path d="M80.0,250.0 L80.0,300.0" class="thin"/><line x1="68" y1="240.0" x2="92" y2="240.0" class="thin"/><line x1="68" y1="250.0" x2="92" y2="250.0" class="thin"/><path d="M80,300 L80,312 M69,312 L91,312 M73,317 L87,317 M77,322 L83,322" class="thin"/><text x="96.0" y="252.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >10 µF +</text><text x="96.0" y="266.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >100 nF</text><rect x="310" y="340" width="200" height="130" rx="9" class="part"/><text x="410.0" y="392.0" class="title" text-anchor="middle" >AHT20</text><text x="410.0" y="410.0" class="sub" text-anchor="middle" >black · I2C 0x38 · 2.7-5.5 V</text><text x="410.0" y="426.0" class="sub" text-anchor="middle" >on two hooks at the top</text><circle cx="340" cy="340" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="340.0" y="348.0" class="pin" text-anchor="end" transform="rotate(-90 340 348)">VIN</text><path d="M340.0,340.0 L340.0,288.0 A8,8 0 0 1 340.0,272.0 L340.0,258.0 A8,8 0 0 1 340.0,242.0 L340.0,228.0 A8,8 0 0 1 340.0,212.0 L340.0,190.0" class="rod"/><circle cx="340.0" cy="190.0" r="6" class="joint"/><circle cx="380" cy="340" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="380.0" y="348.0" class="pin" text-anchor="end" transform="rotate(-90 380 348)">GND</text><path d="M380.0,340.0 L380.0,288.0 A8,8 0 0 1 380.0,272.0 L380.0,258.0 A8,8 0 0 1 380.0,242.0 L380.0,220.0" class="rod"/><circle cx="380.0" cy="220.0" r="6" class="joint"/><circle cx="430" cy="340" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="430.0" y="348.0" class="pin" text-anchor="end" transform="rotate(-90 430 348)">SDA</text><path d="M430.0,340.0 L430.0,288.0 A8,8 0 0 1 430.0,272.0 L430.0,250.0" class="rod"/><circle cx="430.0" cy="250.0" r="6" class="joint"/><circle cx="480" cy="340" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="480.0" y="348.0" class="pin" text-anchor="end" transform="rotate(-90 480 348)">SCL</text><path d="M480.0,340.0 L480.0,280.0" class="rod"/><circle cx="480.0" cy="280.0" r="6" class="joint"/><rect x="100" y="480" width="240" height="200" rx="9" class="part"/><text x="220.0" y="500.0" class="title" text-anchor="middle" >MAX98357A amp</text><text x="220.0" y="518.0" class="sub" text-anchor="middle" >blue · hidden behind the screen</text><text x="112.0" y="666.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >GAIN open = 9 dB</text><text x="112.0" y="652.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >2.5-5.5 V in</text><circle cx="340" cy="540" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="330.0" y="545.0" class="pin" text-anchor="end" >BCLK</text><circle cx="340" cy="570" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="330.0" y="575.0" class="pin" text-anchor="end" >LRC</text><circle cx="340" cy="600" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="330.0" y="605.0" class="pin" text-anchor="end" >DIN</text><circle cx="340" cy="630" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="330.0" y="635.0" class="pin" text-anchor="end" >SD</text><circle cx="100" cy="560" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="110.0" y="565.0" class="pin" text-anchor="start" >OUT+</text><circle cx="100" cy="600" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="110.0" y="605.0" class="pin" text-anchor="start" >OUT−</text><circle cx="230" cy="680" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="230.0" y="672.0" class="pin" text-anchor="start" transform="rotate(-90 230 672)">GND</text><circle cx="300" cy="680" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="300.0" y="672.0" class="pin" text-anchor="start" transform="rotate(-90 300 672)">VIN</text><path d="M560.0,540.0 L340.0,540.0" class="rod"/><text x="450.0" y="533.0" class="lab" text-anchor="middle" >BCLK</text><path d="M560.0,570.0 L340.0,570.0" class="rod"/><text x="450.0" y="563.0" class="lab" text-anchor="middle" >LRC</text><path d="M560.0,600.0 L340.0,600.0" class="rod"/><text x="450.0" y="593.0" class="lab" text-anchor="middle" >DIN</text><path d="M560.0,630.0 L340.0,630.0" class="rod"/><text x="450.0" y="623.0" class="lab" text-anchor="middle" >SD</text><path d="M400.0,630.0 L400.0,644.0 L409.0,646.7 L391.0,652.0 L409.0,657.3 L391.0,662.7 L409.0,668.0 L391.0,673.3 L400.0,676.0 L400.0,690.0" class="thin"/><circle cx="400.0" cy="630.0" r="6" class="joint"/><path d="M400,690 L400,702 M389,702 L411,702 M393,707 L407,707 M397,712 L403,712" class="thin"/><text x="414.0" y="664.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >R1 4.7 kΩ</text><rect x="8" y="520" width="72" height="100" rx="9" class="part"/><text x="44.0" y="556.0" class="title" text-anchor="middle" >Speaker</text><text x="44.0" y="574.0" class="sub" text-anchor="middle" >8 Ω · black</text><circle cx="80" cy="560" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><circle cx="80" cy="600" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><path d="M80.0,560.0 L100.0,560.0" class="thin"/><path d="M80.0,600.0 L100.0,600.0" class="thin"/><text x="44.0" y="636.0" class="fn" text-anchor="middle" >own leads</text><path d="M300.0,740.0 L900.0,740.0" class="bus"/><circle cx="300.0" cy="740.0" r="6" class="joint"/><text x="600.0" y="730.0" class="brass" text-anchor="middle" >BAT+ rail · 3.0-4.2 V from the cell · 26 AWG white</text><path d="M300.0,680.0 L300.0,740.0" class="rod"/><path d="M230.0,680.0 L230.0,720.0" class="rod"/><path d="M230,720 L230,732 M219,732 L241,732 M223,737 L237,737 M227,742 L233,742" class="thin"/><path d="M360.0,740.0 L360.0,765.0" class="thin"/><path d="M360.0,775.0 L360.0,800.0" class="thin"/><line x1="348" y1="765.0" x2="372" y2="765.0" class="thin"/><line x1="348" y1="775.0" x2="372" y2="775.0" class="thin"/><circle cx="360.0" cy="740.0" r="6" class="joint"/><path d="M360,800 L360,812 M349,812 L371,812 M353,817 L367,817 M357,822 L363,822" class="thin"/><text x="376.0" y="776.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >220 µF</text><path d="M760.0,640.0 L760.0,740.0" class="rod"/><circle cx="760.0" cy="740.0" r="6" class="joint"/><path d="M830.0,640.0 L830.0,680.0" class="rod"/><path d="M830,680 L830,692 M819,692 L841,692 M823,697 L837,697 M827,702 L833,702" class="thin"/><rect x="440" y="780" width="170" height="90" rx="9" class="part"/><text x="525.0" y="806.0" class="title" text-anchor="middle" >16340 cell</text><text x="525.0" y="824.0" class="sub" text-anchor="middle" >NL169 · 950 mAh · in the tray</text><circle cx="480" cy="780" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="492.0" y="772.0" class="pin" text-anchor="start" >+ red</text><circle cx="610" cy="850" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="598.0" y="855.0" class="pin" text-anchor="end" >− black</text><path d="M610.0,850.0 L650.0,850.0" class="rod"/><path d="M650,850 L650,862 M639,862 L661,862 M643,867 L657,867 M647,872 L653,872" class="thin"/><text x="650.0" y="888.0" class="fn" text-anchor="middle" >the star</text><rect x="690" y="780" width="190" height="90" rx="9" class="part"/><text x="785.0" y="810.0" class="title" text-anchor="middle" >Toggle</text><text x="785.0" y="828.0" class="sub" text-anchor="middle" >MTS-102 · middle lug in, outer lug out</text><text x="785.0" y="844.0" class="sub" text-anchor="middle" >lever forward = on · charge with it ON</text><circle cx="730" cy="780" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="742.0" y="772.0" class="pin" text-anchor="start" >in</text><circle cx="840" cy="780" r="4.5" class="pinend"/><text x="852.0" y="772.0" class="pin" text-anchor="start" >out</text><path d="M480.0,780.0 L480.0,760.0 L730.0,760.0 L730.0,780.0" class="rod"/><path d="M840.0,780.0 L840.0,740.0" class="rod"/><circle cx="840.0" cy="740.0" r="6" class="joint"/><text x="940.0" y="300.0" class="h2" text-anchor="start" >The power chain</text><text x="940.0" y="322.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >cell → toggle → BAT+ rail → XIAO BAT+ pad and amp VIN</text><text x="940.0" y="338.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >the XIAO's regulator makes 3.3 V for itself, the camera,</text><text x="940.0" y="354.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >the screen and the sensor; the amp runs on the cell itself</text><text x="940.0" y="370.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >returns: amp and XIAO to the holder's − lead (the star);</text><text x="940.0" y="386.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >screen, sensor, button, R1 to the XIAO's GND pin</text><text x="940.0" y="402.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >USB-C in, toggle ON: the XIAO's charger fills the cell</text><text x="940.0" y="436.0" class="h2" text-anchor="start" >From the 950 mAh cell</text><text x="940.0" y="458.0" class="lab" text-anchor="start" >camera streaming, assistant talking</text><text x="940.0" y="473.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >250 mA · about 3.4 h</text><text x="940.0" y="492.0" class="lab" text-anchor="start" >idle on Wi-Fi, screen on</text><text x="940.0" y="507.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >110 mA · about 7.8 h</text><text x="940.0" y="526.0" class="lab" text-anchor="start" >deep sleep, toggle on</text><text x="940.0" y="541.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >5 mA · about a week</text><text x="940.0" y="560.0" class="lab" text-anchor="start" >charging: USB-C into the XIAO, toggle ON, asleep</text><text x="940.0" y="575.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >100 mA · about 10 h from empty</text><text x="940.0" y="594.0" class="lab" text-anchor="start" >external 16340 charger (optional, not owned)</text><text x="940.0" y="609.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >500 mA · about 2 h; pull the cell</text><text x="940.0" y="650.0" class="h2" text-anchor="start" >Never</text><text x="940.0" y="672.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >the 5V pin · a wire to brass · a scope ground on the speaker</text><text x="940.0" y="688.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >the cell soldered, or charged below 0 °C</text><text x="940.0" y="720.0" class="h2" text-anchor="start" >Meter before the cell goes in</text><text x="940.0" y="742.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >every ring and post against BAT+, GND, 3V3: open</text><text x="940.0" y="758.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >holder red lead to the button top: 3.6-4.2 V</text><text x="940.0" y="774.0" class="fn" text-anchor="start" >amp SD to GND: 4.7 kΩ · BAT+ to GND: open, not a short</text><text x="20.0" y="916.0" class="sub" text-anchor="start" >Rev B, 2026-11-10, approved as drawn 2026-11-10: the sphere's first wiring sheet. 43 segments, 6 crossings, each drawn as a hop; the clearance check passes.</text><text x="20.0" y="932.0" class="sub" text-anchor="start" >Pins and powers from the Seeed XIAO ESP32S3 wiki, the Adafruit AHT20 and MAX98357A pages, the Same Sky and Nitecore sheets. Not built.</text></svg>
<figcaption>The sphere's first wiring sheet. One rail, the cell itself; the XIAO's regulator feeds the screen and the sensor; the amp runs on the cell. 6 crossings, each a hop. Every pin and voltage checked against the Seeed wiki and the Adafruit pages.</figcaption></figure>

<h2>Pin map</h2>
<div class="tw"><table class=""><tr><th>Header</th><th>GPIO</th><th>Net</th><th>Job</th></tr><tr><td>D0</td><td>1</td><td><code>BCLK</code></td><td>amp BCLK</td></tr><tr><td>D1</td><td>2</td><td><code>LRC</code></td><td>amp LRC</td></tr><tr><td>D2</td><td>3</td><td><code>DIN</code></td><td>amp DIN</td></tr><tr><td>D3</td><td>4</td><td><code>AMP_SD</code></td><td>amp SD, R1 4.7 kΩ to GND</td></tr><tr><td>D4</td><td>5</td><td><code>SDA</code></td><td>OLED SDA and AHT20 SDA</td></tr><tr><td>D5</td><td>6</td><td><code>SCL</code></td><td>OLED SCL and AHT20 SCL</td></tr><tr><td>D6</td><td>43</td><td></td><td>spare (UART0 TX, chatters at boot: leave free)</td></tr><tr><td>D7</td><td>44</td><td><code>BTN</code></td><td>action button to GND, internal pull-up</td></tr><tr><td>D8 / D9 / D10</td><td>7 / 8 / 9</td><td></td><td>spare; the SD slot's SPI, leave free</td></tr><tr><td>3V3</td><td></td><td><code>3V3</code></td><td>OLED VCC, AHT20 VIN: about 25 mA of the regulator's 700</td></tr><tr><td>GND pin</td><td></td><td><code>GND</code></td><td>OLED GND, AHT20 GND, button, R1 (signal grounds)</td></tr><tr><td>BAT+ pad (back)</td><td></td><td><code>BAT+</code></td><td>from the switch; also the amp VIN and the 220 µF</td></tr><tr><td>BAT− pad (back)</td><td></td><td><code>GND</code></td><td>the holder's − lead, the star; also the amp GND and the 220 µF</td></tr><tr><td>5V pin</td><td></td><td></td><td>USB VBUS only: nothing, ever</td></tr><tr><td>camera, mic</td><td>10-18, 38-40, 47, 48; 41, 42</td><td></td><td>inside the Sense board; not on the sheet</td></tr></table></div>

<h2>Every wire, and why</h2>
<div class="tw"><table class=""><tr><th>Net</th><th>From</th><th>To</th><th>Wire</th><th>Why</th></tr><tr><td><code>BAT+</code></td><td>holder + lead (red)</td><td>toggle middle lug; toggle outer lug → XIAO BAT+ pad, amp VIN, 220 µF +</td><td>26 AWG white</td><td>3.0-4.2 V straight from the cell. One rail; nothing here needs 5 V. The switch breaks the + lead, so off is off: the only thing still on the cell is its own protection board.</td></tr><tr><td><code>GND</code></td><td>holder − lead (black), the star</td><td>XIAO BAT− pad, amp GND, 220 µF −; the XIAO's GND header pin feeds the OLED GND, AHT20 GND, the button and R1</td><td>26 AWG white to the pads and the amp; 30 AWG white for the signal grounds</td><td>One ground, two solder points: the amp's return goes to the holder's lead, never through the XIAO. The frame is no conductor: nothing is soldered to brass.</td></tr><tr><td><code>3V3</code></td><td>XIAO 3V3 pin</td><td>OLED VCC (10 µF + 100 nF to GND at the pin), AHT20 VIN</td><td>30 AWG white</td><td>The screen and the sensor are the only loads on the XIAO's regulator; the XIAO and its camera take the rest.</td></tr><tr><td><code>SDA / SCL</code></td><td>D4 (GPIO5) / D5 (GPIO6)</td><td>OLED SDA / SCL and AHT20 SDA / SCL</td><td>30 AWG white</td><td>The XIAO's hardware I2C pins. Two addresses, 0x3C and 0x38; both boards carry their own pull-ups (4.7 k + 10 k in parallel, 3.2 k: fine at 400 kHz).</td></tr><tr><td><code>BCLK / LRC / DIN</code></td><td>D0 / D1 / D2 (GPIO1 / 2 / 3)</td><td>amp BCLK / LRC / DIN</td><td>30 AWG white</td><td>I2S out only; the microphone is the PDM mic on the Sense board (GPIO41/42), so there is no shared bus. GPIO3 is a strapping pin that only matters if the JTAG eFuse is burned, which it is not on a stock XIAO.</td></tr><tr><td><code>AMP_SD</code></td><td>D3 (GPIO4)</td><td>amp SD, with R1 4.7 kΩ to GND</td><td>30 AWG white</td><td>The amp stays off until the firmware raises SD; the pull-down beats the breakout's 1 MΩ pull-up, so there is no pop at boot.</td></tr><tr><td><code>BTN</code></td><td>D7 (GPIO44)</td><td>button → GND</td><td>30 AWG white</td><td>GPIO44 is UART0 RX, an input at boot, so a button here is harmless. Short press talks, long press resets Wi-Fi.</td></tr><tr><td><code>SPK</code></td><td>amp OUT+ / OUT−</td><td>speaker</td><td>its own 60 mm leads</td><td>Neither lead is ground. Never clip a scope ground to either.</td></tr></table></div>

<h2>Power, run time, charge time</h2>
<div class="tw"><table class=""><tr><th>Mode</th><th>mA from the cell</th><th>Time</th></tr><tr><td>camera streaming, assistant talking</td><td>250</td><td>about 3.4 h on 90 % of 950 mAh; the same budget as the camera tower without its motor</td></tr><tr><td>idle on Wi-Fi, screen on</td><td>110</td><td>about 7.8 h</td></tr><tr><td>deep sleep, toggle on</td><td>5</td><td>about a week; the toggle off is months (only the cell's own protection board stays on)</td></tr><tr><td>charging: USB-C into the XIAO, toggle ON, asleep</td><td>100</td><td>about 10 h from empty. The XIAO's charger is set to 100 mA (Seeed's wiki; one datasheet says 50), with no thermistor: room temperature, the first charge watched. Awake, the device draws more than that, so charge it asleep</td></tr><tr><td>external 16340 charger (optional, not owned)</td><td>500</td><td>about 2 h; pull the cell. Thirteen cells are owned, so one is always charged</td></tr></table></div>
<div class="note warn"><span class="lbl">Carried over, unchanged</span>
<ul>
<li>The cell is the only source. Nothing into the XIAO's <code>5V</code> pin; only the holder on the BAT pads.</li>
<li>Amp off until firmware raises SD; volume cap 65; GAIN open.</li>
<li>Neither speaker lead is ground. No GND wire, no scope ground.</li>
<li>The brass is not a conductor: meter frame-to-every-net before the cell goes in, and after every solder session.</li>
<li>Never solder to the cell; never charge it below 0 °C; watch the first charge.</li>
</ul></div>

<h2>Frame cut list</h2>
<div class="tw"><table class=""><tr><th>Piece</th><th>Stock</th><th>Length</th><th>How</th></tr><tr><td>Equator ring</td><td>1.5 mm rod</td><td>220 mm</td><td>Bend around a 66 mm can, lap-join the ends 8 mm, file flush. Mark left, right, front and back.</td></tr><tr><td>Side ring</td><td>1.5 mm rod</td><td>220 mm</td><td>Same size. It crosses the equator at left and right and runs over the top and under the bottom, so the front stays open.</td></tr><tr><td>Base ring</td><td>1.5 mm rod</td><td>138 mm</td><td>22 mm radius, around a 42 mm jar. It sits at y = −27 touching the side ring at its two low points; the sphere stands on it and the cell tray rests on it.</td></tr><tr><td>Front posts x2</td><td>1.0 mm rod</td><td>50 mm each</td><td>Straight up from the base ring at x = ±11.5 (the OLED's hole pitch, measured), 18.8 mm in front of the centre, to y = 23, the top of the XIAO. Through the OLED's two holes on each side; the XIAO's short edges glued to them.</td></tr><tr><td>Equator ties x2</td><td>1.0 mm rod</td><td>15 mm each</td><td>From each post at y = 3.5, just above the screen's top edge, forward and a little down to the equator at y = 0.</td></tr><tr><td>AHT20 hooks x2</td><td>1.0 mm rod</td><td>12 mm each</td><td>A J: down 3 mm from the side ring at x = ±10.15, forward 6.35 mm, down through the sensor board's front hole, bent under. Solder the top to the ring.</td></tr></table></div>
<div class="note tip"><span class="lbl">Bending a true ring</span>
<p>Wrap the 1.5 mm rod one full turn around a 66 mm can (a 12 oz drink can); it springs back to about 70 mm. Overlap the ends 8 mm side by side, solder the lap, file it round, and put the joint where the base ring will cover it. Check against a 70 mm circle drawn with a compass. The base ring wraps around a 42 mm jar.</p></div>

<h2>Test every part before any brass</h2>
<p>Eight breadboard steps, each with a pass line. They use Seeed's own examples, so no firmware has to exist yet. Do them in order; each adds one part to the last.</p>
<div class="tw"><table class="tests"><tr><th>Step</th><th>Do</th><th>Pass when</th></tr><tr><td>1 · XIAO alone</td><td>USB-C to the laptop. Flash Seeed's CameraWebServer example (XIAO ESP32S3 Sense board, PSRAM on). Join its Wi-Fi page.</td><td>Live video in the browser. Camera, Wi-Fi, PSRAM and the USB port proven.</td></tr><tr><td>2 · Microphone</td><td>Flash Seeed's PDM record example; speak at the board.</td><td>A waveform that follows your voice in the serial plotter.</td></tr><tr><td>3 · OLED</td><td>Breadboard: OLED VCC-3V3, GND-GND, SDA-D4, SCL-D5. I2C scan, then a text sketch.</td><td>Scan shows 0x3C; text on the glass.</td></tr><tr><td>4 · AHT20 on the same bus</td><td>Add the AHT20's VIN/GND/SDA/SCL pads to the same four lines. Scan, then read.</td><td>Scan shows 0x38 and 0x3C; room temperature; humidity jumps when you breathe on it.</td></tr><tr><td>5 · Amp + speaker</td><td>Amp VIN-3V3 (bench only), GND, BCLK-D0, LRC-D1, DIN-D2, SD-D3 with R1 to GND; speaker on OUT+/OUT−. Play a 440 Hz tone at volume 65.</td><td>A clean tone; silence while SD is low. Nothing else wired to the speaker.</td></tr><tr><td>6 · Button</td><td>D7 to GND through the button; internal pull-up in the sketch.</td><td>A press prints once, no bounce after a 30 ms debounce.</td></tr><tr><td>7 · Cell</td><td>Meter the holder: red lead to the button top, 3.6-4.2 V. Toggle in the + lead (middle lug in, outer lug out), then to the XIAO's BAT+ pad; black lead to BAT−. Unplug USB.</td><td>Boots from the cell. Meter in series: 110-250 mA awake, under 5 mA in deep sleep. Then USB in with the toggle ON and the device asleep: about 100 mA into the cell, the charge LED on, nothing warm.</td></tr><tr><td>8 · All together on the breadboard</td><td>Everything from 1-7 at once for an hour, camera streaming.</td><td>No brownout, no reboot, XIAO warm not hot. Only now bend brass.</td></tr></table></div>

<h2>Build order</h2>
<ol><li>Bench-test every part first (the eight steps). Nothing goes near brass untested.</li><li>Measure the OLED&#x27;s hole pitch and the XIAO&#x27;s width with the calipers; set the post spacing to the holes.</li><li>Bend the three 1.5 mm rings and lap-join each. Check the two big ones on a 70 mm circle drawn with a compass.</li><li>Solder the side ring into the equator at left and right (the two crossings), then the base ring to the bottom of the side ring. Harris acid flux, then baking soda, then IPA, as on the first frame. Five joints.</li><li>Set it on the table: it must stand still. Lay the cell tray across the base ring and check it self-rights.</li><li>Solder the two posts to the base ring, straight up, and the two ties from the posts to the equator. Hang the two hooks from the top of the side ring. Meter: every rod is one piece of metal and nothing else touches it.</li><li>Wire the boards first, on the bench, in white: the OLED&#x27;s four, the AHT20&#x27;s four, the amp&#x27;s six, the button&#x27;s two, the BAT pair, all to the XIAO. Kapton on the XIAO&#x27;s back under the antenna.</li><li>Slide the OLED down the posts through its holes to 3 mm above the base ring; a dab of B-7000 at each hole. Seat the XIAO above it with its short edges on the posts; two dabs each side. Lay the wire bundle down behind the boards.</li><li>Tape the toggle to the tray&#x27;s front wall, lever out to the right, and the amp to the back of the screen with Kapton between, its bottom edge level with the screen&#x27;s. Tray onto the ring with two white ties; speaker taped across the tray&#x27;s walls over the cell, grille up; the 220 µF taped to the tray&#x27;s back wall; AHT20 onto its hooks; button glued inside the right joint, cap out.</li><li>Meter frame-to-every-net before the cell goes in, then again after every solder session. First power-up on USB with the toggle OFF, then on the cell. Run the test-8 sketch again inside the sphere.</li></ol>

<h2>Mass</h2>
<div class="tw"><table class=""><tr><th>Part</th><th>g</th></tr><tr><td>Cell + tray</td><td>23</td></tr><tr><td>XIAO ESP32-S3 Sense</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>OLED</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>Speaker</td><td>3.5</td></tr><tr><td>Amp + 220 µF</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>AHT20</td><td>1.5</td></tr><tr><td>Switch + button</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>1.5 mm rod, 3 rings, 580 mm</td><td>8.7</td></tr><tr><td>1.0 mm rod, 154 mm</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Total</strong></td><td><strong>58</strong></td></tr></table></div>

<h2>What could go wrong</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Two rings meeting at a right angle</strong> is the only fiddly joint: hold the side ring upright in the equator with two clothes pegs on a cardboard disc, tack one crossing, check square, tack the other.</li>
<li><strong>The screen's holes.</strong> If the module in the drawer has no holes, or a pitch the posts cannot match, the fallback is two dabs of glue at the screen's edges, as for the XIAO.</li>
<li><strong>The screen's board colour</strong> is the one open colour question: check it in the drawer. Blue would show as a thin frame around the glass.</li>
<li><strong>Wi-Fi.</strong> Three rods with 35 mm gaps are no cage at 2.4 GHz; lay the XIAO's antenna flat on its back, under Kapton, pointing up.</li>
<li><strong>Glue carries the XIAO.</strong> Four dabs on a 0.5 mm gap hold 8 g with margin, but let them cure a day before the sphere is handled.</li>
<li><strong>It rolls.</strong> Knocked off its base ring, a sphere rolls; the low cell brings it back upright. Test the self-righting with the cell in before wiring.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
</div>
